## Project context for iteration estimation

This project has two codelines, both on **vitest** (`vitest run`) and **typescript** (`tsc --noEmit`):

- **mocka** (`/home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-a`) — ticket **MOCK3-1**: riders aged exactly 65 are charged the adult fare instead of the concession fare. The defect is in `src/fares.ts`, where `fareFor` uses `rider.age > 65` instead of `>= 65`. The existing test suite (`test/fares.test.ts`) covers age 70 but has no boundary test at age 65, so a new test case is expected alongside the one-line operator fix.
- **mockb** (`/home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-b`) — ticket **MOCK3-2**: the departure board omits the final stop. The defect is in `src/schedule.ts`, where `formatStops` loops `i < stops.length - 1` instead of `i < stops.length`. The existing test suite (`test/schedule.test.ts`) checks for the arrow separator and the first stop name but does not assert the final stop appears, so a new test case is expected alongside the loop-bound fix.

Both fixes are single-operator changes in small TypeScript files with co-located vitest tests. No build step beyond `tsc --noEmit`; no lint configuration. Estimate iterations with these scopes in mind.

